## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: dashboard/pages/04_payment_terms.py — add import: from dashboard.components.charts import scatter_bubble (add to existing import line from dashboard.components.charts).
- Edit file: dashboard/pages/04_payment_terms.py — add function _spend_terms_scatter(df: pd.DataFrame) -> list[str]. Logic: (1) Guard: if df.empty or 'payment_terms_days' not in df.columns: st.info('No data.'); return []. (2) Filter: has_terms = df[df['payment_terms_days'].notna() & (df['base_amount'] > 0)]. If has_terms.empty: return []. (3) Aggregate: agg = has_terms.groupby('canonical_supplier_name').agg(annual_spend=('base_amount','sum'), avg_terms=('payment_terms_days','mean'), txn_count=('transaction_id','count'), primary_cat=('category_l1', lambda x: x.mode().iloc[0] if not x.dropna().empty else 'Other')).reset_index(). (4) Rename: agg.rename(columns={'canonical_supplier_name':'Supplier','annual_spend':'Annual Spend (AUD)','avg_terms':'Avg Payment Terms (days)','txn_count':'Transaction Count','primary_cat':'Category'}, inplace=True). (5) Call: fig = scatter_bubble(agg, x='Annual Spend (AUD)', y='Avg Payment Terms (days)', size='Transaction Count', color='Category', label='Supplier', title='Supplier Spend vs Payment Terms', hover_name='Supplier'). (6) Add reference lines: fig.add_hline(y=30, line_dash='dash', line_color='grey', annotation_text='30d', annotation_position='right'); fig.add_hline(y=45, line_dash='dash', line_color='orange', annotation_text='45d target', annotation_position='right'). (7) Render with: event = st.plotly_chart(fig, on_select='rerun', key='pt_spend_scatter', use_container_width=True). (8) Extract selections: points = (event or {}).get('selection', {}).get('points', []); selected = [p.get('text') for p in points if p.get('text')]; if selected: st.caption(f'Cross-filter active: {", ".join(selected[:3])} — click chart background to clear'). (9) Return selected.
- Edit file: dashboard/pages/04_payment_terms.py — in main(), call the scatter and set up cross-filter. After the _kpi_row call, insert: st.markdown('---'); st.subheader('Supplier Spend vs Payment Terms'); selected_suppliers = _spend_terms_scatter(filtered); cf = filtered[filtered['canonical_supplier_name'].isin(selected_suppliers)] if selected_suppliers else filtered.
- Edit file: dashboard/pages/04_payment_terms.py — in main(), change _working_capital_table and _non_standard_terms to use cf instead of filtered. Keep _terms_histogram and _supplier_terms_heatmap using filtered (they show the full distribution, not cross-filtered).
- Run: PYTHONPATH=$(pwd) python3 -m py_compile dashboard/pages/04_payment_terms.py && echo 'syntax OK'

